diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 56a6f74..85a4137 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,4 +1,21 @@
-# AEmulator 0.0.0.3
+# AEmulator 0.0.0.4
+
+### Stability and network (this fork)
+- **Guest network self-check**: shortly after every boot the VM log gets one line that tells whether the guest resolves names through the dnsproxyd bridge and whether ping replies — a silent "no network" becomes visible at once, with its cause (broken DNS bridge vs. filtered ICMP).
+- **Network panel** (VM menu → Network): dnsproxyd query counter, `net.dns1`, a resolving probe, the raw ping output, a verdict line, "Test again" and "Restart netd" (the guest re-creates the socket, the bridge takes it over again).
+- **Root switch is now a real switch**: root off removes every `su` binary from the guest tree at once (the VMOS semantics) and root on puts them back; no su files are seeded while root is disabled. The fake `system/app/Superuser.apk` marker (a text file some firmwares' package manager had to scan at boot) is gone — the su binaries are the only artifacts.
+- **su commands run one at a time** through a worker queue: every su call is a full guest process, and a pile of them squeezed the host app that also runs the DNS proxy and all VM services.
+- **su fails fast**: the script exits immediately when the daemon is not running (root off / VM stopped) instead of waiting up to 15 minutes; the in-guest wait dropped from 900 s to 300 s.
+- **Module install fixes**: the package name and version now come from the host-side APK parse (`getPackageArchiveInfo`) — installing an update to an already-installed module no longer misidentifies it; a module without `xposedmodule` meta-data is logged as such.
+- **Module scope editing** (VM menu → Modules → Scope): the per-module scope list (comma-separated packages), pre-filled with the scope the module declares about itself (meta-data `xposedscope` / assets `xposed_scope`).
+- **"Test root"** in the Superuser panel: a full round trip (`su -c id` through the request file, the daemon and back) with the real output shown inline.
+- **Two APKs per release**: `standard` (replaces the original app.aemu — uninstall it first, its images live in the app's private storage and are lost) and `v0003` (`app.aemu.v0003`, installs next to the original and keeps both sets of images).
+
+### Root and modules (0.0.0.3, this fork, ported from the foreign VMOS app)
+- **Working root for guest apps**: the guest tree ships a plain `su` script (/system/bin, /system/xbin, /sbin); every call becomes a request file that a new host-side daemon (core/SuDaemon.kt) runs as a uid-0 guest process and answers with output + exit code. No kernel, no Magisk, works on every engine (2.3–4.4 QEMU and the native arm64 one).
+- **Superuser panel** (VM menu → Superuser): master root switch, default policy (grant all / ask each / deny all), per-app allow/deny rules, the log of recent requests; "ask" requests pop a dialog in the VM window (60 s of silence = deny). Rules persist next to the image.
+- **Xposed module management** (VM menu → Modules): module APKs are installed into the guest as regular apps and registered (enabled/disabled, version); with an enabled module the boot seeds the framework markers the module/checker apps look for (xposed.prop, XposedBridge.jar). The LSPlant in-process loader that applies modules to scoped apps is the next phase; the registry it will consume is live.
+- **APK install fixed**: the "Install APK" menu item pushed the file to the emulated sdcard, which the guest's own pm refuses (like real Android refuses /storage paths) — the dialog then always said "install failed". Now the APK lands in the image's /data/local/tmp (the exact path of the `adb install` that worked) and is installed over the same channel, with pm's real output in the toast.
 
